I don't have time to get
into a debate about this, Karen.

749
01:16:01,766 --> 01:16:04,519
I believe I've made myself clear.

750
01:16:04,602 --> 01:16:06,896
You call this clarity?

751
01:16:07,730 --> 01:16:11,568
You don't have a clue what it's like
to communicate with these kids.

752
01:16:12,402 --> 01:16:15,530
And we are losing them to apathy.

753
01:16:17,740 --> 01:16:20,994
To this prescribed nonsense.

754
01:16:21,661 --> 01:16:23,705
They're slipping away.

755
01:16:23,830 --> 01:16:26,874
I am sorry that you have failed.

756
01:16:28,334 --> 01:16:31,045
If you'll excuse me,
I have another appointment.

757
01:16:33,006 --> 01:16:35,300
You can finish out the week.

758
01:16:41,556 --> 01:16:44,601
Fuck!

759
01:17:04,245 --> 01:17:06,331
Good afternoon.

760
01:17:06,414 --> 01:17:10,877
It gives me great pleasure to
announce that the school dance team

761
01:17:11,085 --> 01:17:15,340
has been invited to perform
on Ed McMahon's "Star Search '88"

762
01:17:15,423 --> 01:17:18,134
in Los Angeles, California.

763
01:17:52,502 --> 01:17:54,504
No, it was ridiculous...

764
01:17:54,587 --> 01:17:56,631
I'll call you back.

765
01:17:57,757 --> 01:18:00,510
- Rose.
- Kitty.

766
01:18:01,302 --> 01:18:06,182
I'm sure you're aware of the horrible
allegations against Jim Cunningham.

767
01:18:06,307 --> 01:18:09,644
I know, I saw it on TV.
Something about a kiddie porn...

768
01:18:09,852 --> 01:18:13,189
Oh, please! Don't use those words!

769
01:18:13,898 --> 01:18:18,027
It's obviously a conspiracy
to destroy an innocent man.

770
01:18:18,152 --> 01:18:23,074
I am going to spearhead the
Jim Cunningham defence campaign.

771
01:18:24,826 --> 01:18:29,163
Rose, I have to appear
at his arraignment tomorrow morning.

772
01:18:29,330 --> 01:18:33,418
The girls are scheduled to leave
for Los Angeles in the morning.

773
01:18:33,543 --> 01:18:37,797
As their coach, I was the
obvious choice to chaperone them...

774
01:18:37,880 --> 01:18:40,758
But now you can't go.

775
01:18:40,842 --> 01:18:42,510
- Yes.
- Hm.

776
01:18:42,635 --> 01:18:45,304
Now, believe me,
of all the other mothers,

777
01:18:45,430 --> 01:18:47,432
I would never dream of asking you.

778
01:18:47,515 --> 01:18:50,768
But none of the other mothers
are available to go.

779
01:18:52,979 --> 01:18:55,064
I don't know, Kitty.

780
01:18:55,148 --> 01:18:58,151
It's a bad weekend.
Eddie's in New York.

781
01:18:58,276 --> 01:19:02,488
Rose, I don't know if you realise

782
01:19:02,613 --> 01:19:06,284
what an opportunity this is
for our daughters.

783
01:19:06,367 --> 01:19:11,414
This has been a dream of Samantha's
and all of ours for a long time.

784
01:19:12,081 --> 01:19:14,917
I made her lead dancer.

785
01:19:15,835 --> 01:19:20,631
Sometimes I doubt your commitment
to Sparkle Motion.

786
01:19:50,745 --> 01:19:53,372
Elizabeth will be in charge.

787
01:19:53,456 --> 01:19:56,042
She'll drive you to therapy.

788
01:19:56,834 --> 01:20:01,172
And if you need anything, promise me
you will call Dr Thurman.

789
01:20:11,766 --> 01:20:15,645
How does it feel
to have a wacko for a son?

790
01:20:20,483 --> 01:20:22,568
It feels wonderful.

791
01:21:03,442 --> 01:21:06,904
What do I tell the others
when they ask about you?

792
01:21:08,990 --> 01:21:11,742
Tell them everything
is gonna be just fine.

793
01:21:13,828 --> 01:21:16,289
What's "cellar door"?

794
01:21:16,414 --> 01:21:19,709
This famous linguist once said

795
01:21:19,792 --> 01:21:23,504
that of all the phrases
in the English language,

796
01:21:23,629 --> 01:21:27,925
of all the endless combinations
of words in all of history,

797
01:21:28,009 --> 01:21:31,637
that "cellar door" is the most beautiful.

798
01:21:33,973 --> 01:21:36,559
"Cellar door"?

799
01:22:07,340 --> 01:22:11,886
I promise that one day
everything's gonna be better for you.

800
01:22:14,180 --> 01:22:16,265
Shut up!

801
01:22:29,070 --> 01:22:33,324
- I want to talk about your past today.
- No.

802
01:22:33,407 --> 01:22:37,995
I want to talk
about you and your parents.

803
01:22:38,120 --> 01:22:41,874
They didn't buy me
what I wanted for Christmas.

804
01:22:42,708 --> 01:22:45,461
What did you want for Christmas
that year?

805
01:22:46,170 --> 01:22:47,964
Hungry Hungry Hippos.

806
01:22:51,092 --> 01:22:55,554
How did you feel, being denied
these Hungry Hungry Hippos?

807
01:22:56,138 --> 01:22:57,640
Regret.

808
01:22:58,349 --> 01:23:01,018
What else makes you feel regret?

809
01:23:02,687 --> 01:23:04,814
That I did it again.

810
01:23:05,773 --> 01:23:07,900
You did it again?

811
01:23:08,609 --> 01:23:13,072
I flooded my school and I
burned down that pervert's house.

812
01:23:15,741 --> 01:23:19,078
I only have a few days
before they catch me.

813
01:23:19,203 --> 01:23:21,580
Did Frank tell you to do these things?

814
01:23:21,706 --> 01:23:24,875
I have to obey him. He saved my life.

815
01:23:25,960 --> 01:23:29,338
I have to obey him
or I'll be left all alone,

816
01:23:29,422 --> 01:23:31,507
and then...

817
01:23:31,632 --> 01:23:36,053
and then I won't be able to figure out
what this is all about.

818
01:23:36,137 --> 01:23:39,598
I won't be able
to know his master plan.

819
01:23:40,474 --> 01:23:43,394
Do you mean God's master plan?

820
01:23:44,729 --> 01:23:47,231
Do you now believe in God?

821
01:23:47,356 --> 01:23:50,067
I have the power
to build a time machine.

822
01:23:50,151 --> 01:23:52,069
How is that possible?

823
01:23:55,448 --> 01:23:59,118
How is time travel possible, Donnie?

824
01:23:59,201 --> 01:24:01,454
Time's up, Frank said.

825
01:24:01,579 --> 01:24:03,789
When is this going to happen?

826
01:24:03,914 --> 01:24:05,916
Soon.

827
01:24:07,501 --> 01:24:10,880
Soon.

828
01:24:25,728 --> 01:24:28,147
What is going to happen?

829
01:24:30,483 --> 01:24:34,028
Frank is gonna kill.

830
01:24:34,153 --> 01:24:36,739
Who is he going to kill?

831
01:24:40,117 --> 01:24:43,662
- Who is he going to kill?
- I can see him right now!

832
01:24:48,709 --> 01:24:51,212
The sky is going to open up.

833
01:24:57,676 --> 01:25:02,264
If the sky were to suddenly open up,
there would be no law.

834
01:25:02,348 --> 01:25:04,266
There would be no rule.

835
01:25:04,350 --> 01:25:07,394
There would only be you
and your memories.

836
01:25:07,561 --> 01:25:12,525
The choices you've made
and the people you've touched.

837
01:25:13,442 --> 01:25:15,486
If this world were to end,

838
01:25:15,569 --> 01:25:19,615
there would only be you and him.

839
01:25:19,740 --> 01:25:21,700
And no-one else.

840
01:25:59,947 --> 01:26:02,032
Hey.

841
01:26:02,116 --> 01:26:04,577
I got in.

842
01:26:05,619 --> 01:26:09,915
I am going to Harvard.

843
01:26:12,293 --> 01:26:14,420
We should totally throw a party.

844
01:26:14,545 --> 01:26:19,049
Mum and Dad are gone. It's
Halloween. We could get away with it.

845
01:26:19,133 --> 01:26:22,511
OK, but it has to be small, all right?

846
01:26:25,764 --> 01:26:27,641
Happy Halloween!

847
01:26:38,319 --> 01:26:40,529
Beelzebub!

848
01:26:55,544 --> 01:26:59,423
We got eggs, water balloons
and a dozen rolls of toilet paper.

849
01:26:59,506 --> 01:27:01,800
I stole four beers from my dad.

850
01:27:01,884 --> 01:27:05,512
- We got a keg.
- Keg beer is for pussies.

851
01:27:22,613 --> 01:27:25,241
'Rose, this is Lilian Thurman.

852
01:27:25,366 --> 01:27:29,620
It is extremely important that you
call me as soon as you hear this.

853
01:27:29,703 --> 01:27:31,830
Thank you.

854
01:27:37,920 --> 01:27:39,838
- Hi.
- Hey.

855
01:27:43,592 --> 01:27:45,094
You OK?

856
01:27:47,554 --> 01:27:49,890
Yeah. My mum's gone.

857
01:27:50,933 --> 01:27:53,185
You wanna come in?

858
01:27:53,310 --> 01:27:55,354
Yeah.

859
01:28:16,917 --> 01:28:21,714
I don't know. She...
She didn't leave a note and...

860
01:28:21,797 --> 01:28:24,049
the house was all messed up.

861
01:28:24,133 --> 01:28:26,260
But you're OK?

862
01:28:29,763 --> 01:28:31,849
Did you call the cops?

863
01:28:32,808 --> 01:28:37,855
Yeah. They said I should leave
the house and go to a safe place.

864
01:28:40,274 --> 01:28:44,987
I'm just so scared. I keep thinking
something awful is happening and...

865
01:28:46,864 --> 01:28:50,200
It's my fucking stepdad. I know it.

866
01:28:59,376 --> 01:29:04,381
I guess some people are just
born with tragedy in their blood.

867
01:29:07,968 --> 01:29:13,307
- Have you guys seen Frank?
- No, I think they went on a beer run.

868
01:29:15,059 --> 01:29:17,478
'If you're there, pick up.

869
01:29:17,603 --> 01:29:21,607
'Hello. Good news.
The girls got three and a half stars

870
01:29:21,690 --> 01:29:24,318
'and get to come back
for the quarterfinals.

871
01:29:24,401 --> 01:29:27,905
'Samantha was amazing. Anyway...

872
01:29:28,030 --> 01:29:31,116
We'll take the red-eye back tonight,
and we...

873
01:29:31,200 --> 01:29:33,327
Mum, the plane's about to leave.

874
01:29:33,410 --> 01:29:37,289
We'll take the red-eye
and should arrive around 8.30.

875
01:29:37,373 --> 01:29:41,710
Um... I hope everything's all right.

876
01:29:41,794 --> 01:29:44,129
I love you. Bye.

877
01:31:30,110 --> 01:31:32,196
'Cellar door.'

878
01:31:39,203 --> 01:31:42,164
- Come with me.
- Where are we going?

879
01:31:42,247 --> 01:31:45,709
- Just tell me.
- Look, we gotta go.

880
01:31:45,792 --> 01:31:49,880
- We have to see Grandma Death.
- Is this about the book?

881
01:31:49,963 --> 01:31:54,384
No, it's Frank. Time is running out.
We gotta go.

882
01:32:24,957 --> 01:32:27,709
Roberta Sparrow.

883
01:32:28,627 --> 01:32:30,879
Grandma Death.

884
01:32:39,304 --> 01:32:43,058
Donnie, nobody's here.
Let's forget about it.

885
01:32:44,643 --> 01:32:47,020
Cellar door.

886
01:32:47,104 --> 01:32:48,981
What?

887
01:33:51,752 --> 01:33:53,670
Donnie!

888
01:33:56,381 --> 01:33:58,925
Donnie!

889
01:33:59,009 --> 01:34:01,094
Why the fuck are you here?

890
01:34:01,720 --> 01:34:03,847
Oh, my God.

891
01:34:05,599 --> 01:34:08,602
- You're dead!
- What do we do with him?

892
01:34:08,727 --> 01:34:10,729
Leave him alone!

893
01:34:14,232 --> 01:34:16,568
Don't fucking move.

894
01:34:18,528 --> 01:34:21,156
Oh, fuck! Aargh!

895
01:34:25,786 --> 01:34:28,872
There's a car!

896
01:34:28,997 --> 01:34:31,792
Get the hell out of here! Now!

897
01:34:32,584 --> 01:34:35,212
Seth, there's a car coming! Let's go!

898
01:34:35,295 --> 01:34:38,590
- I have a bigger knife now.
- God!

899
01:34:40,133 --> 01:34:42,969
Let's go! Here come the cops!

900
01:34:46,640 --> 01:34:49,101
Did you call the fucking cops?

901
01:34:49,184 --> 01:34:51,978
<i>- Deus ex machina.</i>
- What did you say?

902
01:34:53,772 --> 01:34:57,025
- What the fuck did you say?
- Our saviour.

903
01:35:01,613 --> 01:35:03,782
Donnie!

904
01:35:15,752 --> 01:35:17,838
Gretchen?

905
01:35:22,300 --> 01:35:24,386
Gretchen?

906
01:35:25,929 --> 01:35:28,306
Gretchen.

907
01:35:31,143 --> 01:35:33,270
Wake up, Gretchen.

908
01:35:33,395 --> 01:35:35,397
Frank.

909
01:35:35,480 --> 01:35:38,358
- Wake up.
- What did you do?

910
01:35:40,026 --> 01:35:42,863
Gretchen, wake up. Wake up.

911
01:35:42,988 --> 01:35:44,990
Wake up.

912
01:35:46,992 --> 01:35:49,119
Gretchen?

913
01:35:49,244 --> 01:35:51,246
Gretchen.

914
01:35:51,371 --> 01:35:53,832
What the fuck did you do, man?

915
01:35:55,041 --> 01:35:57,419
You killed her, Frank!

916
01:36:00,422 --> 01:36:02,549
Is she dead?

917
01:36:10,515 --> 01:36:13,018
What were you guys doing
in the road?

918
01:36:13,101 --> 01:36:15,228
What were you thinking?

919
01:36:22,486 --> 01:36:24,196
Go home!

920
01:36:25,155 --> 01:36:28,700
Go home and tell your parents
everything'll be OK.

921
01:36:29,493 --> 01:36:31,536
Go!

922
01:38:37,662 --> 01:38:39,998
'28 days,

923
01:38:40,832 --> 01:38:42,751
'six hours...'

924
01:38:43,543 --> 01:38:45,754
42 minutes,

925
01:38:46,671 --> 01:38:48,924
12 seconds.

926
01:38:53,178 --> 01:38:55,305
I'm going home.

927
01:39:13,031 --> 01:39:15,325
'To travel back in time,

928
01:39:15,408 --> 01:39:18,828
'you have to have a spaceship
that can travel faster than light.'

929
01:39:18,912 --> 01:39:22,832
- 'Theoretically.'
- 'And be able to find a wormhole.'

930
01:39:22,916 --> 01:39:27,087
'The principles of time travel are
there. You've got a vessel, a portal.

931
01:39:27,170 --> 01:39:30,757
'The vessel can be anything.
Probably a spacecraft.

932
01:39:30,882 --> 01:39:32,926
'A metal craft of any kind.'

933
01:39:44,396 --> 01:39:47,816
'What if you could go back in time

934
01:39:47,941 --> 01:39:50,777
'and take all those hours
of pain and darkness

935
01:39:50,860 --> 01:39:53,780
'and replace them
with something better?'

936
01:40:37,282 --> 01:40:39,909
'Dear Roberta Sparrow,

937
01:40:40,035 --> 01:40:41,953
'I've reached you in your book

938
01:40:42,078 --> 01:40:45,248
'and there's so many things
I need to ask you.

939
01:40:46,207 --> 01:40:49,294
'Sometimes I'm afraid
of what you might tell me.

940
01:40:53,298 --> 01:40:57,385
'Sometimes I'm afraid you'll tell me
this is not a work of fiction.

941
01:40:58,845 --> 01:41:03,683
'I can only hope the answers
will come to me in my sleep.

942
01:41:04,601 --> 01:41:07,437
'I hope that when the world
comes to an end,

943
01:41:07,520 --> 01:41:09,856
'I can breathe a sigh of relief

944
01:41:09,939 --> 01:41:13,526
'because there will be so much
to look forward to.'

945
01:45:44,505 --> 01:45:46,424
Hey.

946
01:45:46,507 --> 01:45:48,551
What's going on?

947
01:45:48,676 --> 01:45:53,473
Horrible accident.
My neighbour... got killed.

948
01:45:54,599 --> 01:45:56,642
What happened?

949
01:45:56,726 --> 01:45:58,936
Got smooshed by a jet engine.

950
01:46:04,817 --> 01:46:07,070
What was his name?

951
01:46:07,153 --> 01:46:09,739
Donnie. Donnie Darko.

952
01:46:09,864 --> 01:46:11,908
Hmm.

953
01:46:11,991 --> 01:46:14,494
I feel bad for his family.

954
01:46:15,328 --> 01:46:17,413
Yeah.

955
01:46:24,045 --> 01:46:26,130
Did you know him?

956
01:46:29,050 --> 01:46:31,135
No.
